cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CGE-Core, please cite it as below, and additionally cite the
  original PyCGE (Fung & Burtwistle, NIST) and the Hosoe, Gasawa & Hashimoto
  (2010) textbook whose models it implements. Users of the IFPRI subsystem
  should also cite the separately obtained IFPRI Standard CGE documentation
  and source package. See README.md ("Provenance and license") for details.
title: "CGE-Core: a Pyomo-based computable general equilibrium framework"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Miraflor
    given-names: James Matthew
    email: james.miraflor@gmail.com
version: 0.4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/miraflor/CGE-core"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cge
  - computable-general-equilibrium
  - pyomo
  - economics
  - policy-simulation
notes: >-
  CGE-Core is a corrected and annotated fork of PyCGE by Juan Fung and
  Charley Burtwistle (U.S. National Institute of Standards and Technology,
  2017; public domain under 17 U.S.C. 105). The inherited PyCGE/Hosoe model
  port is not the fork maintainer's original work. The IFPRI Standard CGE
  subsystem was independently written within this fork from public
  mathematical descriptions; the official IFPRI source package and test data
  remain external. The fork's revisions were produced through an AI-assisted
  ("vibecoded") workflow directed and reviewed by James Matthew Miraflor. The
  inherited model equations were checked line-by-line against the GAMS Model
  Library reference implementations (splcge.gms SEQ=275, stdcge.gms SEQ=276),
  while the IFPRI benchmark and five policy simulations are checked against
  full-precision external reference runs. The regression suite validates the
  numerical benchmarks and workflow behaviour.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "PyCGE: A Python Interface for Solving CGE Models"
    authors:
      - family-names: Fung
        given-names: Juan
      - family-names: Burtwistle
        given-names: Charley
    year: 2017
    url: "https://github.com/juanfung/pycge"
    institution:
      name: "National Institute of Standards and Technology"
  - type: book
    title: >-
      Textbook of Computable General Equilibrium Modelling: Programming and
      Simulations
    authors:
      - family-names: Hosoe
        given-names: Nobuhiro
      - family-names: Gasawa
        given-names: Kenji
      - family-names: Hashimoto
        given-names: Hideo
    year: 2010
    publisher:
      name: "Palgrave Macmillan"
    doi: "10.1057/9780230281653"
